'' ANDROID ON ARM64 LINKS AS ON x86-64 -- the arch comes from the triple, aarch64's builtins from the NDK (docs/tiko-android A3).
'' ANDROID LINKS AGAINST THE NDK (docs/tiko-android A1 step 3): its sysroot for Bionic's stubs and
'' crt objects, its clang's resource directory for libclang_rt.builtins and libunwind.a, and
'' '-lm -ldl' -- no -lpthread (the NDK has none; pthreads are in libc) and no -ltinfo (Android has
'' no terminfo). The NDK here (src/fakendk) is a stand-in holding only what discovery checks, and the library
'' path has no fbrt0.o, so the line is printed and the link stops: exit 5.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_ANDROID_NDK=tests/driver/src/fakendk
'' ARGS: -v -target android-arm64 tests/driver/src/no-fbrt0.bas -p tests/driver/src/elfgroup -o build/.andndk64-never
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 5
'' EXPECT-OUT-SEQ: -target aarch64-linux-android29 -fuse-ld=lld
'' EXPECT-OUT-SEQ: --sysroot="tests/driver/src/fakendk/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/
'' EXPECT-OUT-SEQ: -resource-dir "tests/driver/src/fakendk/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/
'' EXPECT-OUT-SEQ: -Xlinker --start-group
'' EXPECT-OUT-SEQ: -lm -ldl
'' EXPECT-OUT-SEQ: -Xlinker --end-group
'' EXPECT-NOT: -ltinfo
'' EXPECT-NOT: -lpthread
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.andndk64-never
